WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.709
Metadata, licenses, and gated access.

2
00:00:02.989 --> 00:00:06.659
The card’s top section is YAML metadata between two --- lines.

3
00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:11.632
The fields you will use most are license (an identifier such as apache-2.

4
00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:23.219
0 or mit ), base_model (for fine-tunes, adapters, quantizations, and merges), datasets, pipeline_tag (the task, such as text-generation ), library_name, and tags.

5
00:00:23.499 --> 00:00:34.763
When the license is not on the Hub’s list, the card says license: other, puts the text in a LICENSE file, and gives the license a name in license_name (and often a link in license_link ).

6
00:00:35.043 --> 00:00:42.189
Because the metadata is machine-readable, you can audit a shortlist of models in code before anyone downloads gigabytes.

7
00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:43.941
Some repos are gated.

8
00:00:44.221 --> 00:00:53.331
You must be logged in and request access, often by accepting the license and filling in fields such as your name, affiliation, and intended use.

9
00:00:53.611 --> 00:00:59.243
The publisher configures approval as automatic or manual; manual approval can take days.

10
00:00:59.523 --> 00:01:11.917
The card metadata can customize the gate with extra_gated_prompt and extra_gated_fields, and a gated repo can set extra_gated_eu_disallowed: true to refuse requests from the EU.

11
00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:18.384
Meta’s Llama and Muse repos and some others are gated; Apache-licensed releases often are not.

12
00:01:18.664 --> 00:01:20.435
Datasets work the same way.

13
00:01:20.715 --> 00:01:31.829
The datasets library loads a dataset by its Hub name ( load_dataset("org/name") ), can stream large datasets instead of downloading them, and caches what it downloads.

14
00:01:32.109 --> 00:01:48.536
A dataset card plays the role of a model card; the practice echoes “Datasheets for Datasets” by Gebru and colleagues (2018), which argued every dataset should document its motivation, composition, collection process, and recommended uses.

15
00:01:48.816 --> 00:01:54.917
Read a dataset’s license and its collection description before you train on it, which you will do in week 2.
